  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1241 PM CDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nThe upper high will continue its slow westward trek Wednesday before \neventually settling over the Desert Southwest by late week. This \nwill both allow for temps to gradually cool through the week and \nbring higher rain chances. The first good chance for rain comes late \nWednesday. Models are in good agreement with a shortwave trough \nbringing a cold front across the central CONUS and through the FA by \nlate Wednesday morning. The front is still in place just to our west \nas a weakness rotates around the upper high and helps convection \ndevelop. Remnants of this front remain in the area through late \nweek and remain a source for daily thunderstorm chances across the\nFA. Unfortunately rain chances look to mostly come to an end by \nthe weekend as the upper high moves back over Texas as it \ntransits towards the southeast CONUS. While this will bring some \nincrease in temperatures, the upper high will not be as strong as \nit is today (Monday).",
